 "internal_silences": [],
 "text": "Last spring, I started a small garden on my balcony. I had no experience, and I had very little space. So I began with three pots, some soil and a few seeds. I chose herbs, because they grow quickly and they smell wonderful. Every evening, I checked the soil with my finger. If it felt dry, I gave the plants some water. Within a month, the first leaves appeared. By summer, I was cooking with my own basil and mint. The garden taught me patience. It also taught me that small efforts, repeated every day, can bring real results. If you have a window, you have room to start."
